  Say the word if either should be different.

  [1m6. Browser UI[0m

  The existing [38;5;153mindex.html[39m becomes a FastAPI-served template: a login form, a task list, and inline create/edit. Plain
  [38;5;153mfetch[39m and plain JS — no build step, no framework. It's a thin client over the API, and it stays that way so #4 can add
  a notification bell without fighting a rendering layer.

  [1m7. Project layout, tooling, testing[0m

  A [38;5;153muv[39m project with [38;5;153mpyproject.toml[39m and a project-local [38;5;153m.venv[39m (per your Python rules — nothing installed into the global
  [38;5;153mmain[39m env).

  src/tasks_app/{main,db,models,auth}.py
  src/tasks_app/services/tasks.py
  src/tasks_app/api/{auth,tasks}.py
  src/tasks_app/static/
  tests/

  [38;5;153mruff[39m + [38;5;153mruff format[39m, [38;5;153mmypy[39m, and [38;5;153mpytest[39m wired up before feature code, with one passing fixture to prove the harness runs.
  Tests use [38;5;153mhttpx.AsyncClient[39m against a temp-file SQLite database — hermetic, no network, no shared state. Development
  follows TDD per your workflow.

  [1m8. Explicitly out of scope[0m

  Notifications of any kind, watchers, email, WebSocket/SSE, roles and permissions, password reset, rate limiting,
  deployment. Each is either a later sub-project or a deliberate omission to name in the spec.

